    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0422" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg402"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 16, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: This department is in possession of
                    authentic information that among the persons who recently committed piracy and
                    murder on board the United States steamer Chesapeake were two named Braine and
                    Parr, respectively, and that they have taken refuge in the British province of
                    New Brunswick or Nova Scotia. As it is desirable that they should be detained
                    there until the formal affidavits can be forwarded with a view to their
                    extradition for trial in this country, I will thank you to request her Majesty’s
                    authorities to do anything which can be legally done for that purpose.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, my lord, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD. </signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
